{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs7FoyeezBXoktW3h1F4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BzRmLxMa9wxti2Er57v8Ri","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-medium-r1/cases/t16_json_patch/jsonpatch/SPEC.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11805,"cache_read_input_tokens":10397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11805},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4970d8d6-7876-442e-86f0-9362ede8454c","uuid":"f6ab16d4-f876-490c-ab10-038928091800","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:07:11.127Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs7FoiH7vMNZkPu5cHZF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BzRmLxMa9wxti2Er57v8Ri":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-medium-r1/cases/t16_json_patch/jsonpatch/SPEC.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BzRmLxMa9wxti2Er57v8Ri","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Spec\n2\t\n3\t## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)\n4\t\n5\t`resolve_pointer(doc, pointer) -> value`\n6\t\n7\t- `\"\"` is the whole document. Otherwise the pointer starts with `/` and each token is\n8\t  unescaped: `~1` -> `/`, `~0` -> `~` (in that order).\n9\t- Object tokens are keys. Array tokens must be a non-negative integer with no leading\n10\t  zeros (`\"0\"` ok, `\"01\"` not ok); `\"-\"` is only valid for `add` as \"append\".\n11\t- Anything invalid raises `PointerError` (subclass of `PatchError`).\n12\t\n13\t## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)\n14\t\n15\t`apply_patch(doc, patch, in_place=False) -> new_doc`\n16\t\n17\t`patch` is a list of operation dicts with `op` in `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,\n18\t`copy`, `test`, plus `path` and, where applicable, `value` or `from`.\n19\t\n20\t- `add`: object key set or array insert at index (index == len allowed, `-` appends);\n21\t  replacing the root is allowed.\n22\t- `remove`: target must exist.\n23\t- `replace`: target must exist.\n24\t- `move`: `from` must exist; `from` must not be a proper prefix of `path` (cannot move a\n25\t  value into one of its own children); equivalent to remove then add.\n26\t- `copy`: `from` must exist; deep copy; then add.\n27\t- `test`: deep equality of `value` with the target. Numbers compare by value\n28\t  (`1 == 1.0`), but `True != 1`.\n29\t- Operations apply in order. If any operation fails, raise `PatchError` and leave the\n30\t  input document unchanged (atomic). With `in_place=True` the input document is mutated\n31\t  on success and untouched on failure; otherwise the input is never mutated.\n32\t- Unknown `op`, missing required fields, or wrong types raise `PatchError`.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4970d8d6-7876-442e-86f0-9362ede8454c","uuid":"cd790914-0e20-4f19-bb57-1a9ad1fc047c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:07:11.203Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-medium-r1/cases/t16_json_patch/jsonpatch/SPEC.md","content":"# Spec\n\n## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)\n\n`resolve_pointer(doc, pointer) -> value`\n\n- `\"\"` is the whole document. Otherwise the pointer starts with `/` and each token is\n  unescaped: `~1` -> `/`, `~0` -> `~` (in that order).\n- Object tokens are keys. Array tokens must be a non-negative integer with no leading\n  zeros (`\"0\"` ok, `\"01\"` not ok); `\"-\"` is only valid for `add` as \"append\".\n- Anything invalid raises `PointerError` (subclass of `PatchError`).\n\n## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)\n\n`apply_patch(doc, patch, in_place=False) -> new_doc`\n\n`patch` is a list of operation dicts with `op` in `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,\n`copy`, `test`, plus `path` and, where applicable, `value` or `from`.\n\n- `add`: object key set or array insert at index (index == len allowed, `-` appends);\n  replacing the root is allowed.\n- `remove`: target must exist.\n- `replace`: target must exist.\n- `move`: `from` must exist; `from` must not be a proper prefix of `path` (cannot move a\n  value into one of its own children); equivalent to remove then add.\n- `copy`: `from` must exist; deep copy; then add.\n- `test`: deep equality of `value` with the target. Numbers compare by value\n  (`1 == 1.0`), but `True != 1`.\n- Operations apply in order. If any operation fails, raise `PatchError` and leave the\n  input document unchanged (atomic). With `in_place=True` the input document is mutated\n  on success and untouched on failure; otherwise the input is never mutated.\n- Unknown `op`, missing required fields, or wrong types raise `PatchError`.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BzRmLxMa9wxti2Er57v8Ri","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
