{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs7JjA2PP4xurfVAzbny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`jsonpatch/core.py` now implements `resolve_pointer` and `apply_patch` per the spec. My 39 tests in `tests/test_core.py` all pass.\n\n- **Pointers:** `~1` is unescaped before `~0`. Array tokens must be non-negative integers with no leading zeros. `-` is accepted only as an append position for `add`; everywhere else it raises `PointerError`.\n- **Atomicity:** `apply_patch` always works on a deep copy, so a failure leaves the input untouched. With `in_place=True`, a dict or list root is overwritten after the whole patch succeeds, and the same object is returned. If the root is replaced by a different type, the new document is returned instead and the input is left alone.\n- **`test` comparison:** Numbers compare by value, so `1 == 1.0`. Booleans only equal booleans, so `True != 1`, and this holds inside nested lists and dicts.\n- **`move`:** The proper-prefix check compares tokens, not string prefixes. Moving `/a` to `/ab` is allowed; moving `/a` to `/a/c` raises. Moving a path onto itself does nothing.\n\nThe spec doesn't cover `remove` on the document root (`\"\"`), so I made it raise `PatchError`. Tell me if you'd rather it be allowed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16969,"cache_read_input_tokens":39863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16969},"output_tokens":437,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4970d8d6-7876-442e-86f0-9362ede8454c","uuid":"1499f8b2-6999-4242-b878-6322f4f8351d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:07:52.893Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs7Jiv8PW2bXWrJ95NXd"}
